course: dictionary
lesson: 5273
title: What is Judaism?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Judaism is a religion. A religion is a set of beliefs about God, and a way of living that people share. Judaism is the religion of the Jewish people, and it is one of the oldest religions in the world.
explain: Jewish people believe in one God. Long ago, God made a special promise, called a covenant, with Abraham, and God gave the Torah to Moses. The Torah is very important in Judaism.
explain: The word has a capital J because it is a proper noun, the name of a religion. «Jesus was Jewish, and Christianity grew out of Judaism.» So Judaism came first, and Christianity grew from its roots.
fact: Judaism is the religion of the Jewish people.
fact: Jewish people believe in one God, who made a covenant with Abraham.
fact: In RE you can learn about the synagogue, the rabbi, the Sabbath (Shabbat), kosher food, and festivals such as Passover, Hanukkah, Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur.
fact: «Orthodox Judaism» and «Reform Judaism» are two different styles of Judaism.
exercise: What is Judaism? | A type of food only | A kind of weather | A king who lived long ago | *The religion of the Jewish people
exercise: How many Gods do Jewish people believe in? | None | *One | Many | Two
exercise: Who was given the Torah by God? | Abraham | *Moses | Mary | Jesus
test: «Christianity grew out of Judaism.» In this sentence, which religion came first? | Christianity | *Judaism | Hinduism | Islam
test: Which place do Jewish people go to pray and learn? | Gurdwara | Church | *Synagogue | Mosque
exam: Which of these is the name of the holy book given to Moses? | *Torah | Vedas | Quran | Bible
